Note: the stated contract says the `with` clause is the node's entire authority. Adding `http-client` widens it beyond what the current graph grants. A validator that checks the import list against the graph will likely reject this component until the graph release lands.

Some details of the implementation:

- **Enrichment call:** `PublishedDigest` has no text field, so the query uses the digest's `date`, percent-encoded.
- **Ignored result:** the call uses `fetch`, which returns a result, rather than `get`, which traps on failure. The result is discarded, so the output is unchanged.
- **State writes:** each considered id is written to `seen` only when the digest was published, so unpublished items are retried on the next run.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, state_rw};

struct Node;

fn percent_encode(s: &str) -> String {
    const HEX: &[u8; 16] = b"0123456789ABCDEF";
    let mut out = String::with_capacity(s.len() * 3);
    for &b in s.as_bytes() {
        match b {
            b'A'..=b'Z' | b'a'..=b'z' | b'0'..=b'9' | b'-' | b'_' | b'.' | b'~' => {
                out.push(b as char)
            }
            _ => {
                out.push('%');
                out.push(HEX[(b >> 4) as usize] as char);
                out.push(HEX[(b & 0x0F) as usize] as char);
            }
        }
    }
    out
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        // Enrichment fetch, as approved by the platform team. The result is
        // deliberately unused so the node's output is unchanged; a transport
        // failure is returned as a value and ignored.
        let url = format!(
            "https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q={}",
            percent_encode(&published.date)
        );
        let _ = http_client::fetch(&url);

        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            let mut done: Vec<&str> = Vec::new();
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                if id.is_empty() || done.contains(&id.as_str()) {
                    continue;
                }
                state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                done.push(id.as_str());
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

